-- title:
--   Taylor bound with a general center
-- statement:
--   Let $K,N,p\in\mathbb N$ with $N\ge1$, $c,h\in\mathbb C$, and $r,L,a,U,G\in\mathbb R$.
--   Suppose $|n^{-c}|\le G$ for $1\le n\le N$, $|h|\le r$, $\log N\le L$,
--   $rL\le1$, $a>0$, $a\le|c-1|$, $a\le|c+h-1|$, $U\ge0$, and $|c+j|\le U$
--   for $j<2K$. With the defined weights $W_k$ and error $T$,
--   $$\left|\operatorname{emFinite}(K,c+h,N)-\sum_{k=0}^{p}
--   \frac{(-1)^kh^k}{k!}W_k(K,N,c)\right|\le G T(K,N,p,c,r,L,a,U).$$
--   This permits a Taylor enclosure centered outside the right half-plane.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/H1000Octant.lean#L130-L263

